Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["InfraMetricTensor", "ObjectName",
 CellID->1224892054,ExpressionUUID->"8393d601-4014-44ba-afc9-60862df940ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"72757b2f-b719-4761-ba87-e8848e605117"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraMetricTensor"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMetricTensor", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9fddd58b-2852-460e-98d2-2fb49712a05e"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "gives the matrix over all pairs of vertices ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 " of ",
 StyleBox["d(p,u) / d(p,v)", "TI"],
 ", where ",
 StyleBox["u", "TI"],
 " is the vertex of the interval ",
 StyleBox["I(p,w)", "TI"],
 " closest to ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ". Rows and columns follow ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"VertexList", "[", "g", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "42ccd285-217f-441c-bac0-5b4b7c6a78c4"],
 ".",
 "\n",
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"84384944-d285-4c80-9668-7862e546cc11"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraMetricTensor"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMetricTensor", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0dd5d181-ae60-49eb-895d-131ec87982ae"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "gives the same matrix restricted to the shell ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["FindInfraShell"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraShell", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "65f3e981-b351-4512-8fd3-0f2767c47f99"],
 ", in the order of that shell."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"47210007-83e7-4bdd-a06b-638dbcf05abc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Definition: the interval is ",
 StyleBox["I(p,w) = {u : d(p,u) + d(u,w) = d(p,w)}", "TI"],
 ", the vertices on some geodesic from ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 ". The foot of ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " on it is a vertex ",
 StyleBox["u", "TI"],
 " of the interval at least distance from ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ". The entry is the distance of the foot from the base, over the distance of \
",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " from the base:"
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e4891be9-cdd9-4ea0-9013-28af06e265a6"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["T[v, w] = d(p,u) / d(p,v)", "TI"]], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"6b84b5a4-853f-4756-9cb5-c674623479ab"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Rows are ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ", the projected vertex; columns are ",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 ", the end of the interval."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"1184cb41-c50a-4951-b254-55131039751b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In the plane, the nearest point of the segment ",
 StyleBox["[p,w]", "TI"],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " lies at distance ",
 StyleBox["clamp(|v| cos \[Theta], 0, |w|)", "TI"],
 " from ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 ", where \[Theta] is the angle at ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 ". So ",
 StyleBox["T = clamp(cos \[Theta], 0, |w|/|v|)", "TI"],
 ", and on a circle about ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " it is ",
 StyleBox["max(0, cos \[Theta])", "TI"],
 ": the Gram matrix of the unit directions, with every angle of 90\[Degree] \
or more read as 0. This is Euclid's projection of Book II, Propositions 12 \
and 13."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b2bbe2d7-84f4-43bb-8c8e-d345c5bce630"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The row of ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " is 0, the column of ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " is 0, and the diagonal off ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " is 1. Every entry satisfies ",
 StyleBox["0 \[LessEqual] T[v,w] \[LessEqual] d(p,w)/d(p,v)", "TI"],
 ". The matrix is not symmetric in general; on a shell it is symmetric on the \
square grid."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"aa28b33b-e6a5-4021-b8a7-edfaddd57e94"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "On the square grid the interval is a box and the foot is the coordinate \
clamp, unique. Then ",
 StyleBox["T[v,w] = (d(p,v) + d(p,w) \[Minus] d(v,w)) / (2 d(p,v))", "TI"],
 ", the Gromov product of ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["w", "TI"],
 " at ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " over ",
 StyleBox["d(p,v)", "TI"],
 ". On a shell of radius ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " this is ",
 StyleBox["1 \[Minus] d(v,w)/(2r)", "TI"],
 " at every radius. The tensor is scale-invariant on the grid, so it does not \
approach the cosine as the radius grows: two diagonal directions at a right \
angle read 1/2, where the plane reads 0."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"299c95f0-4a43-4049-9afe-68ffd10acaad"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "On a periodic tiling the rescaled path metric tends to a polyhedral norm, \
not the Euclidean one, and the tensor tends to the projection tensor of that \
norm. It approaches ",
 StyleBox["max(0, cos \[Theta])", "TI"],
 " only on substrates whose large-scale metric is round, such as a fine \
isotropic mesh."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"29147754-8c0e-4596-bc7f-3c20e402e3dd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The foot need not be unique. Where the large-scale norm has flat faces, as \
on the triangular tiling, ",
 StyleBox["d(v, \[CenterDot])", "TI"],
 " is constant along whole stretches of the interval, and many vertices tie. \
Option ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<SelectCoordinate\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58c05f5e-314b-48c2-b8db-4e79dbe3b88b"],
 " says which index ",
 StyleBox["d(p,u)", "TI"],
 " of the tied feet is kept:"
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0bbfc7bc-d885-4617-bf42-9ef8c9ad1686"],

